    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nOPEN VIEWINGS: \nWednesday 23rd between 4.30pm - 5pm. \n\n12 College View is a well-presented three-bedroom mid-terrace home that comes to the market in good condition throughout, while still offering purchasers the opportunity to put their own stamp on it. \n\nIdeally located at the top of Blarney Street, the property enjoys a convenient and highly sought-after setting close to Strawberry Hill and Shanakiel, with a host of local amenities, schools, and transport links nearby, while Cork City Centre is just a short distance away.\n\nThis home benefits from off-street parking for one car to the front and enjoys pleasant views across the city from the doorstep. Accommodation comprises an entrance hallway, living room, kitchen/dining area, and understairs storage on the ground floor. Upstairs, there are three bedrooms and a main family bathroom.\n\nTo the rear lies a spacious garden, mainly laid to lawn, providing excellent outdoor space and plenty of potential for future landscaping, or extension opportunities (subject to planning).\n\nConveniently located at the top of Blarney Street, the home enjoys easy access to a wealth of local amenities, including schools, shops, recreational facilities, and Cork city centre. This mature residential area offers a strong sense of community, with local shops, pubs, and a community centre all nearby. Cork city centre is approximately a 25-minute walk away, while regular bus services are available within a short walk of No. 12.\n\n12 College View is an ideal purchase for first-time buyers, downsizers, or investors seeking a home in a convenient city location with further scope to personalise and add value.\n\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all that this property has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nWelcoming entrance hallway with wood effect linoleum flooring, providing access to all ground floor accommodation and benefiting from understairs storage.\n\nLiving Room - 2.96m x 2.5m\nPositioned to the front of the home, this bright south facing living room features an open fireplace, two windows with partial plantation shutters, and built-in shelving.\n\nKitchen/Dining - 5.00m x 3.20m\nSpacious open-plan kitchen/dining room with tiled flooring, two windows overlooking the rear garden, and a glass door providing direct access outside. The kitchen is fitted with an excellent range of floor and eye-level units, complemented by a laminate wood worktop and marble tiled splashback. A central island provides additional storage and workspace. The kitchen also includes an oven and hob and is fitted with a high-quality washing machine and condenser dryer. The dining area comfortably accommodates a family-sized table and chairs.\n\nLanding - \nBright landing providing access to three bedrooms, the main bathroom, hot press, and attic storage.\n\nBathroom - 1.8m x 1.9m\nSpacious bathroom comprising a three-piece shower suite, fully tiled walls and floor, and a frosted rear-facing window.\n\nBedroom 1 - 2.7m x 3.5m\nGenerous front-facing bedroom featuring a spacious built-in wardrobe and two windows overlooking the front of the property, enjoying attractive city views.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.2m x 3.2m\nWell-proportioned rear-facing bedroom featuring a spacious built-in wardrobe and two windows overlooking the rear garden\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.3m x 2.5m\nFront-facing bedroom with timber flooring and fitted shelving.\n\n"
      },
